    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>\"Magic is grammar. Reality is a draft.\"</em></p><p>You are a prepared, academic manifestant who edits meaning directly. You do not delegate power; you channel it raw.</p><p><strong>Engine truth:</strong> your craft runs on <strong>Clarity</strong> (your casting pool, deeper than other paths), <strong>Noise</strong> (the lattice hears sloppy work), <strong>Surge</strong> (the editor's one currency — +1 at the start of your turn), and <strong>Blood Debt</strong> (reaching above your tier, discounted by your Discipline). <em>The cast dialog's cost line is the truth.</em></p><p><em>An earlier draft of this class spoke of Resonance, Strain, and correspondence alignment. Those pools were folded into Surge — the fiction survives; the bookkeeping does not.</em></p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
